" Modal's built-in command file: the default key bindings. It runs first, then modalrc in
" your config directory, which can change any of it. modal --write-config FILE writes every
" setting, binding and colour there is, to start from. keysection "TITLE" starts a group of
" keys in the list of keys (, ?).

" Moving the cursor
keysection "Moving the cursor"
nmap h          cursor-left       "Left"
nmap <Left>     cursor-left       "Left"
nmap j          cursor-down       "Down"
nmap <Down>     cursor-down       "Down"
nmap k          cursor-up         "Up"
nmap <Up>       cursor-up         "Up"
nmap l          cursor-right      "Right"
nmap <Right>    cursor-right      "Right"
nmap 0          cursor-first      "First field"
nmap <Home>     cursor-first      "First field"
nmap $          cursor-last       "Last field"
nmap <End>      cursor-last       "Last field"
nmap gg         go-first          "First event, or bar {count}"
nmap G          go-last           "End, or bar {count}"

" Moving in time, to the event at or after where each lands, in the track's bars: the same
" place a bar on, a bar line, a chord (events starting within chordwindow of each other), a
" section's start, a marker
keysection "Moving in time"
nmap }          cursor-bar-next           "Same place, next bar"
nmap {          cursor-bar-previous       "Same place, bar before"
nmap ]b         cursor-bar-line-next      "Next bar line"
nmap [b         cursor-bar-line-previous  "Bar line before"
nmap )          cursor-chord-next         "Next chord"
nmap (          cursor-chord-previous     "Chord before"
nmap ]s         cursor-section-next       "Next section"
nmap [s         cursor-section-previous   "Section before"
nmap ]m         cursor-marker-next        "Next marker"
nmap [m         cursor-marker-previous    "Marker before"

" The piano roll: k and j move a semitone, K and J an octave (J joins sections on the
" section strip), and Tab and Shift-Tab go to the next note's start at any pitch and the one
" before, notes starting together low to high
keysection "Pitch in the piano roll"
nmap K          octave-up                 "Up an octave"
nmap <Tab>      cursor-note-next          "Next note"
nmap <S-Tab>    cursor-note-previous      "Note before"

" The piano roll's grid and default note, each track's own and saved with it: zh and zl (or z
" with Left and Right) make the grid finer and coarser, its steps narrower and wider as h and l
" go left and right; Ctrl-T turns triplets on and off; and
" , n takes the current note's length and velocity as the default note, which o adds. :grid
" and :len set them by length, such as 1/8 or 1/16t.
keysection "The grid and default note"
nmap zh         grid-finer                "Finer grid"
nmap z<Left>    grid-finer                "Finer grid"
nmap zl         grid-coarser              "Coarser grid"
nmap z<Right>   grid-coarser              "Coarser grid"
nmap <C-t>      grid-triplets             "Triplets on or off"
nmap <leader>n  note-default              "Default note from this one"

" Changing events: Enter edits the field under the cursor, typing a value or a change such
" as +10 or +1/16 (Enter sets it, Escape leaves it); + and - (or Ctrl-A and Ctrl-X) step it,
" with counts; in the piano roll, Ctrl-A and Ctrl-X step the current note's velocity. d and
" y take a range, up to a boundary its key names (d]b up to the next bar line, d]s the next
" section, dG the end, dj this event and the next), or an object: ib this bar's events, ab
" this bar as time, which d takes out, closing the gap up to the section's end, and in the
" note or event under the cursor. dd and yy are this bar's events; x deletes the note or
" event under the cursor and Y yanks it. p lays what was yanked or deleted over what's
" there, and P puts it in, moving the rest of the section later; bars go to the start of the
" cursor's bar. u and Ctrl-R undo and redo.
keysection "Changing events"
nmap <CR>       field-edit        "Edit this field"
nmap +          field-increase-fine "Step up"
nmap =          field-increase    "Step up"
nmap <C-a>      number-increase   "Step up"
nmap -          field-decrease    "Step down"
nmap _          field-decrease-fine "Step down"
nmap <C-x>      number-decrease   "Step down"
nmap d          operator-delete   "Delete"
nmap y          operator-yank     "Yank"
nmap x          event-delete      "Delete this event"
nmap p          register-put      "Put"
nmap P          register-put-before "Put before"
nmap Y          yank-this         "Yank this"
keysection "After an operator"
omap ib         object-bar-contents "This bar's events"
omap ab         object-bar        "This bar, as time"
omap in         object-note       "This note"
keysection "Changing events"
nmap o          note-add          "Add a note"
nmap O          note-add-advance  "Add a note and move on"
nmap u          undo              "Undo"
nmap <C-r>      redo              "Redo"

" Tracks: the conductor's list is track 0, before track 1
keysection "Tracks"
nmap gt         track-next        "Next track, or track {count}"
nmap gT         track-previous    "Track before"

" Scrolling. Ctrl with a direction moves the cursor and scrolls with it, so it stays in
" place on screen, until the view can't scroll further.
keysection "Scrolling"
nmap <C-h>      cursor-left-scroll  "Left, scrolling"
nmap <C-Left>   cursor-left-scroll  "Left, scrolling"
nmap <C-j>      cursor-down-scroll  "Down, scrolling"
nmap <C-Down>   cursor-down-scroll  "Down, scrolling"
nmap <C-k>      cursor-up-scroll    "Up, scrolling"
nmap <C-Up>     cursor-up-scroll    "Up, scrolling"
nmap <C-l>      cursor-right-scroll "Right, scrolling"
nmap <C-Right>  cursor-right-scroll "Right, scrolling"
nmap <C-{>      cursor-bar-previous-scroll "Same place, bar before, scrolling"
nmap <C-S-[>    cursor-bar-previous-scroll "Same place, bar before, scrolling"
nmap <C-}>      cursor-bar-next-scroll "Same place, next bar, scrolling"
nmap <C-S-]>    cursor-bar-next-scroll "Same place, next bar, scrolling"
nmap <C-d>      scroll-half-down  "Half a page down"
nmap <C-u>      scroll-half-up    "Half a page up"
nmap <C-f>      scroll-page-down  "A page down"
nmap <PageDown> scroll-page-down  "A page down"
nmap <C-b>      scroll-page-up    "A page up"
nmap <PageUp>   scroll-page-up    "A page up"
nmap zz         scroll-centre     "Centre the cursor"
nmap zi         zoom-in           "Zoom in"
nmap zo         zoom-out          "Zoom out"
nmap z0         zoom-reset        "Zoom as at the start"
nmap zf         playhead-follow   "Follow the playhead again"

" Views: the arrangement, the piano roll and the event list, each at the cursor, and
" Backspace back to the view before
keysection "Views"
nmap ga         view-arrangement  "Arrangement"
nmap gr         view-piano-roll   "Piano roll"
nmap ge         view-events       "Event list"
nmap <BS>       view-back         "Back"

" The section strip, above the arrangement's tracks: gs goes to it (or k from the first
" track), j back. There, h and l go between sections, x, d, y, Y, p and P delete, yank and
" put them, Alt-h and Alt-l move one, J joins it with the next, + and - lengthen and shorten
" it by a bar, i and a insert a new one, c renames it, and Enter plays from it.
keysection "The section strip"
nmap gs         section-strip     "Section strip"
nmap <A-h>      move-left         "Move earlier"
nmap <A-l>      move-right        "Move later"
nmap J          join              "Join with the next"

" Adding notes in the piano roll: o adds the track's default note at the cursor, and O adds
" it and moves on, past its end, or with gridadvance (, t a) to the next grid step; 8O adds
" eight one after another.
" Moving notes in the piano roll: Alt-h and Alt-l to the grid steps either side, Alt-H and
" Alt-L a nudge (the nudge setting, in milliseconds), Alt-{ and Alt-} a bar, Alt-k and Alt-j
" a semitone, Alt-K and Alt-J an octave, or Alt and Alt-Shift with the arrow keys. = and -
" move its end to the grid steps either side, + and _ a nudge.
keysection "Moving notes"
nmap <A-Left>   move-left         "Move earlier"
nmap <A-Right>  move-right        "Move later"
nmap <A-S-Left> move-left-fine    "Nudge earlier"
nmap <A-S-Right> move-right-fine  "Nudge later"
nmap <A-Up>     move-up           "Up a semitone"
nmap <A-Down>   move-down         "Down a semitone"
nmap <A-S-Up>   move-octave-up    "Up an octave"
nmap <A-S-Down> move-octave-down  "Down an octave"
nmap <A-S-h>    move-left-fine    "Nudge earlier"
nmap <A-S-l>    move-right-fine   "Nudge later"
nmap <A-{>      move-bar-previous "A bar earlier"
nmap <A-S-[>    move-bar-previous "A bar earlier"
nmap <A-}>      move-bar-next     "A bar later"
nmap <A-S-]>    move-bar-next     "A bar later"
nmap <A-k>      move-up           "Up a semitone"
nmap <A-j>      move-down         "Down a semitone"
nmap <A-S-k>    move-octave-up    "Up an octave"
nmap <A-S-j>    move-octave-down  "Down an octave"
nmap i          insert-before     "Insert before"
nmap a          insert-after      "Insert after"
nmap c          change            "Rename"

" The inspector: e edits the fields of the note under the cursor in the piano roll, or the
" section on the section strip, starting on the one it was last on; in the event list it
" edits the field under the cursor in place, as Enter does. Tab and Shift-Tab set the field
" and go to the next or the one before, round from the last to the first; Enter sets it and
" leaves, Escape leaves it; Up and Down step it.
keysection "The inspector"
nmap e          inspector-edit    "Edit in the inspector"

" The leader key, comma unless the leader setting names another, starts the commands used now
" and then. After a pause, the hint menu shows what can follow it, as it does after any keys
" that start longer bindings; ngroup gives such keys their title there. <leader><leader> is
" kept free, for a command used often enough to earn it.
keysection "The leader"
ngroup <leader>  "Leader"
nmap <leader>?   keys-show         "The keys here"
ngroup <leader>v "Views"
nmap <leader>va  view-arrangement  "Arrangement"
nmap <leader>vp  view-piano-roll   "Piano roll"
nmap <leader>ve  view-events       "Event list"
ngroup g         "Go"
ngroup z         "View"
ngroup ]         "Next"
ngroup [         "Before"

" Text size: Ctrl with plus, minus or 0, on the keyboard or the keypad. Plus is shifted on
" most keyboards, so Ctrl-= and Ctrl-Shift-= are bound too.
keysection "Text size"
nmap <C-=>      font-bigger       "Bigger text"
nmap <C-S-=>    font-bigger       "Bigger text"
nmap <C-+>      font-bigger       "Bigger text"
nmap <C-kPlus>  font-bigger       "Bigger text"
nmap <C-->      font-smaller      "Smaller text"
nmap <C-kMinus> font-smaller      "Smaller text"
nmap <C-0>      font-reset        "Text size from the config"
nmap <C-k0>     font-reset        "Text size from the config"

" The command line: : opens it, and in it these keys edit, run and recall lines. Other
" characters are typed.
keysection "The command line"
nmap :          command-line            "Command line"
cmap <CR>       command-line-run        "Run"
cmap <Esc>      command-line-cancel     "Cancel"
cmap <BS>       command-line-backspace  "Delete back"
cmap <Del>      command-line-delete     "Delete"
cmap <Left>     command-line-left       "Left"
cmap <Right>    command-line-right      "Right"
cmap <Home>     command-line-start      "Start"
cmap <End>      command-line-end        "End"
cmap <C-u>      command-line-clear      "Clear"
cmap <Up>       command-line-older      "Older line"
cmap <Down>     command-line-newer      "Newer line"
cmap <Tab>      command-line-next       "Next field"
cmap <S-Tab>    command-line-previous   "Field before"

nmap <Esc>      cancel            "Cancel"

" Playing: Space plays from the play-from marker (the ▶ in the margin), or stops; m Space puts
" the marker at the cursor, and Ctrl-Space puts it there and plays. With rewind (on by
" default) the marker stays put; without, it moves to where playback stops. , t Space turns
" rewind on or off.
" Ctrl-. panics, in every mode: All Notes Off and Reset All Controllers on every channel.
keysection "Playing"
nmap <Space>    play-toggle       "Play or stop"
nmap <C-Space>  play-cursor       "Play from the cursor"
nmap m<Space>   marker-set        "Play from here"
ngroup <leader>t "Toggles"
nmap <leader>t<Space> rewind-toggle "Rewind on or off"
nmap <leader>ta  grid-advance-toggle "O by grid step or note length"
nmap <C-.>      panic             "Panic"
cmap <C-.>      panic             "Panic"
